<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <div class="text-center">
    <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <.back_link href={home_path()} />
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-black text-base-content">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted max-w-narrow mx-auto">
      Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
      disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our application and use our
      services.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 max-w-narrow mx-auto space-y-8">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Information We Collect</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc ps-6 space-y-2 text-muted">
        <li>
          Account details (email, provider IDs): stored when you sign up or sign in with OAuth
          providers like Discord, Google, Facebook, GitHub, Apple or Steam.
        </li>
        <li>
          Service activity needed to run the app, such as logins, sessions, game activity, and
          account-related events.
        </li>
        <li>
          Content you choose to share, such as your display name, avatar, chat messages, and
          leaderboard entries. This content is visible to other players.
        </li>
        <li>
          Reports you send about a problem, from the report form or the game: what you write, the
          page or item it is about, any screenshot you add, your browser and screen size, and an
          email address if you give one. Screenshots are seen only by the site's admins. A report
          is deleted 180 days after it is closed, and with your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          Network information such as IP address, processed transiently for security, rate limiting,
          abuse prevention, and approximate country-level request statistics. If an IP address is
          banned for abuse, it is stored until the ban is lifted or expires.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc ps-6 space-y-2 text-muted">
        <li>To authenticate and identify you when you log in.</li>
        <li>To provide, operate and maintain our services.</li>
        <li>
          To communicate with you about changes, updates, support, and security.
        </li>
        <li>
          To protect the service from spam, abuse, automated attacks, and excessive traffic.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        We use cookies and local storage for core app features and payments, such as sessions,
        remember-me login, CSRF protection, theme preference, banner dismissal, game
        authentication tokens, and the last page you visited in the tab (so the report form can
        fill it in). We do not use analytics cookies, advertising cookies, or third-party
        tracking cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        We use third-party services that collect or process personal data on our behalf. Depending
        on which features are turned on, these include:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc ps-6 mt-2 space-y-2 text-muted">
        <li>OAuth sign-in providers, when you sign in with one.</li>
        <li>Stripe, which processes payments made on the website.</li>
        <li>Platform stores (Apple, Google, Steam), when you make a purchase in an app.</li>
        <li>
          A human-verification service (Cloudflare Turnstile) on the sign-up and email sign-in
          forms, which receives your IP address and browser details.
        </li>
        <li>
          An email delivery provider, which receives your email address to send sign-in links,
          confirmations and account messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          Push notification services (Apple Push Notification service, Firebase Cloud Messaging),
          which receive your device's push token when you allow notifications.
        </li>
        <li>Error monitoring, to diagnose crashes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Please review those providers' privacy policies for details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Data Retention &amp; Security</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        We keep personal data as long as necessary for service operation and to comply with legal
        obligations. We use reasonable safeguards to protect your data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
      <p :if={@contact_email} class="text-muted">
        You may request access, correction, or deletion of your personal data by emailing <a
          href={"mailto:" <> @contact_email}
          class="link link-primary"
        >{@contact_email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p :if={!@contact_email} class="text-muted">
        You may request access, correction, or deletion of your personal data by contacting us
        through the app or support channels.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Contact</h2>
      <p :if={@contact_email} class="text-muted">
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, email us at <a
          href={"mailto:" <> @contact_email}
          class="link link-primary"
        >{@contact_email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p :if={!@contact_email} class="text-muted">
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us via the project's
        contact channels.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="text-center pt-8 border-t border-base-300">
      <small class="text-xs text-muted">Last updated: September 2026</small>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
